  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Mid-20th-Century Monument to Freedom in Kochani</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One of a series of abstract spomeniks, or monuments built between the 1950s and the 1990s during Tito&apos;s Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, the Monument to Freedom in Kochani commemorates the struggles of Macedonians between the 1903 Ilinden Uprising against Ottoman rule and the events of World War II. This project involves the comprehensive restoration of the monument.</narrative>
  </description>
